Fix a duplicate declaration that breaks any build with CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER.

kernel/trace/trace_event_perf.c declares `struct perf_event *event;` twice inside
perf_ftrace_function_call(). The enclosing #ifdef CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER is never
compiled in the shipped miatoll_defconfig, so the tree builds as published, but
enabling the function tracer (needed to match the export set of the kernel that
boots on this device) fails with "redefinition of 'event'".

This is a compiler-error fix only: no behaviour change, no config change.

--- a/kernel/trace/trace_event_perf.c
+++ b/kernel/trace/trace_event_perf.c
@@ -428,7 +428,6 @@
 {
 	struct perf_event *event;
 	struct ftrace_entry *entry;
-	struct perf_event *event;
 	struct hlist_head head;
 	struct pt_regs regs;
 	int rctx;
